# TEACH Ticket System — environment variable reference
#
# This file documents environment-variable NAMES and safe placeholders only.
# Real values belong in a local, git-ignored environment file
# (e.g. .env, .env.local) or in managed deployment secrets — never in this
# file and never committed to source control.
#
# Rules for every future phase:
# - Document new variables here using their NAME and a safe placeholder only
#   (e.g. EXAMPLE_VARIABLE=replace-with-your-value) — never a real value.
# - Real credentials, tokens, keys, or connection strings must never be
#   committed to this repository under any filename.
#
# None of the variables below are required merely to build or preview the
# application — the app builds and runs with none of them set. They are
# only read at request time by explicit database commands or by the
# authentication routes/pages when a request actually needs them.
#
# Once these are configured in a real environment, run
# `npm run readiness:check` to confirm they are structurally valid — it
# never prints the values themselves. See docs/DEPLOYMENT.md.

# Runtime/application PostgreSQL connection (future use).
# DATABASE_URL=postgresql://user:replace-with-your-value@host:5432/database

# Optional direct migration/seed connection. Useful when a provider
# distinguishes a pooled runtime connection from a direct migration
# connection. Migration and seed commands — and the guarded
# `npm run admin:bootstrap` and `npm run access:invite` commands (see
# docs/DEPLOYMENT.md) — prefer this and fall back to DATABASE_URL when it
# is not set. Keep this operator-only; do not add it to Vercel's
# environment variables alongside the running application's own
# configuration.
# DATABASE_MIGRATION_URL=postgresql://user:replace-with-your-value@host:5432/database

# Better Auth session/cookie signing secret. Generate a long random value
# (e.g. `openssl rand -base64 32`) — never reuse this placeholder.
# BETTER_AUTH_SECRET=replace-with-your-value

# The application's own public base URL (used to build OAuth redirect URIs
# and set cookie domain/security attributes). No trailing slash.
# BETTER_AUTH_URL=https://replace-with-your-value.example.com

# Google OAuth 2.0 client credentials for Google sign-in. Issued from a
# Google Cloud project's OAuth client — never a personal Google account
# credential. GOOGLE_CLIENT_SECRET is a secret and must never carry a
# NEXT_PUBLIC_ prefix or be exposed to the browser. In workspace mode this
# is normally a TEACH-owned Google Cloud project's client; in invite_only
# mode it may instead be an External OAuth client controlled outside TEACH
# Workspace, since invited accounts are not required to belong to it.
# GOOGLE_CLIENT_ID=replace-with-your-value
# GOOGLE_CLIENT_SECRET=replace-with-your-value

# Phase 9A: selects which of two authentication-access modes is active.
# Exactly one of the two configurations below — never both, never neither.
# A missing or invalid value leaves authentication unavailable (fails
# closed); there is no permissive default. See docs/AUTHENTICATION.md.
#
# Controlled pilot access — any verified Google account may sign in, but
# only if the address has a current invitation (see `npm run access:invite`
# and the /admin Pilot Invitations section):
# AUTH_ACCESS_MODE=invite_only
#
# Strict TEACH Workspace access — only verified @teachps.org Google
# Workspace accounts may sign in (requires AUTH_ALLOWED_DOMAIN below):
# AUTH_ACCESS_MODE=workspace

# Required only when AUTH_ACCESS_MODE=workspace. The exact Google Workspace
# domain allowed to sign in. For the TEACH deployment this is teachps.org.
# AUTH_ALLOWED_DOMAIN=teachps.org

# Phase 9B: temporary, security-conscious public ticket intake. Enables
# /requests/new to accept a new IT or Facilities request from an
# unauthenticated visitor while Google OAuth is unavailable — never a
# general authentication bypass, and it never makes any ticket list, ticket
# detail, comment, support, account, or admin route public. Only the exact
# literal value "true" enables it; any other value (including absence)
# leaves it disabled and existing authenticated behavior unchanged. See
# docs/AUTHENTICATION.md and docs/DEPLOYMENT.md.
# PUBLIC_TICKET_INTAKE=true

# Required only when PUBLIC_TICKET_INTAKE=true. A separate secret (never
# reuse BETTER_AUTH_SECRET) used to compute a durable, database-backed
# submission rate limiter's pseudonymous fingerprint. Generate a long
# random value (e.g. `openssl rand -base64 32`) of at least 32 characters
# — never reuse this placeholder, and never commit a real value.
# PUBLIC_INTAKE_RATE_LIMIT_SECRET=replace-with-your-value
